    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Mickey Moniak** (75.98) and **James Wood** (73.20) represent our elite-tier offensive anchors. **Mickey Moniak** benefits from a massive confluence of variables: the combination of a favorable park factor (+14%), a soft matchup against Avila (+19% SP skill), and a significant platoon edge against a right-handed starter. Similarly, **James Wood** is set up for success at the top of the order; his elite xwOBA of 0.424, paired with a favorable matchup against P\u00e9rez, makes him our most bankable asset for run production. Meanwhile, **Corbin Carroll** remains a vital inclusion at 61.24. Despite a difficult matchup against Messick, **Corbin Carroll** provides the essential stolen base floor we prioritize as a core team philosophy, even when the daily efficiency score is tempered by the southpaw opponent.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision landed on **Isaac Paredes**, who just missed the cut at 45.88. While **Isaac Paredes** projected well enough to theoretically contribute, he was relegated to the bench primarily due to the daunting task of facing deGrom, whose elite strikeout profile significantly depressed the overall efficiency projection. We opted for the higher-floor matchup equity provided by **Tyler Soderstrom** (63.54) and **Jose Caballero** (63.48), the latter of whom maintains strong startability despite wind-in conditions at the park today. \n\nWe are monitoring risk factors closely across the diamond. **Jose Caballero**, **Seiya Suzuki**, and **Mickey Moniak** are all facing pitchers with high \"Elite Hold\" percentages, which creates a drag on their SB potential for this specific session. Furthermore, while we are confident in the starts for **Gabriel Moreno**, **Josh Naylor**, and **Cole Young**, all three are facing left-handed starters, which requires us to accept a minor \"Dynamic Platoon\" penalty to their base projections. We remain diligent in monitoring the weather for these contests, but as it stands, our lineup is optimized to maximize both raw output and our team\u2019s critical speed profile.",
